# Programs run from their erased terms, the forms still to come (test_theory_run.wap runs the others): a recursion
# runs by its body as written, once the kernel checked that the function equals it, and a call of itself in last
# place runs as a loop, an exit as a jump.
# Source: notes/coc-plan.md S2 and 9.7 "What runs", wiki/function.md
use "../check.wap"
use "scripted.wap"
check("a recursion runs by its body", both_ways("factorial", "factorial(n: int): int := if n == 0 then 1 else n * factorial(n - 1)\nfactorial(5)"), "120\nexit 0")
check("a call of itself in last place runs as a loop, deep without overflow", both_ways("count", "count(n: int, total: int): int := if n == 0 then total else count(n - 1, total + 1)\ncount(1000000, 0)"), "1000000\nexit 0")
check("a block returns early", both_ways("early", "first_big(a: int, b: int): int := { if a > 10 { return a }; b }\nfirst_big(20, 3) + first_big(1, 3)"), "23\nexit 0")
